TRANSLATIONS FROZEN
===================

The German, French, Spanish and Italian builds under de/ fr/ es/ it/ were
generated from an earlier revision of the English site. The English homepage
has since been redesigned and rewritten, so those pages are now STALE: they
are structurally valid and grammatically clean, but they no longer say what
index.html says.

They are deliberately left in place rather than deleted, so the URLs and the
translated string files in this directory survive the English rewrite.

While this file exists, the release gate holds stage 6 instead of failing it.

To unfreeze, once the English page is signed off:

    rm i18n/FROZEN
    python3 build_i18n.py
    cd test && bash release.sh ..

The gate will then fail until every localised page matches the new English
structure — which is the point.

SPANISH AND ITALIAN ARE UNLISTED
--------------------------------

Decision, 28 August 2026. The firm states it works in German, French and
English, so the site now offers only those three. es/ and it/ are still built
and still in the repository — nothing is deleted — but they are:

  * absent from the language switcher on every English page
  * absent from the hreflang alternate set and from sitemap.xml
  * served noindex, follow

build_i18n.py carries this as UNLISTED_LANGS, alongside the existing
UNLISTED_PAGES. To republish them on expansion, remove the code from that set
and rebuild; nothing else has to be undone.

The de/ and fr/ pages still list es/ and it/ in their own switchers. They were
not hand-edited, because they are frozen and because their switcher hrefs are
broken independently of this (see below) — regenerating fixes both at once.

KNOWN BUG, NOT INTRODUCED BY THE ABOVE
--------------------------------------

The language switcher on every localised page carries English-relative hrefs:
from /de/services.html, "Deutsch" points at de/services.html, which resolves
to /de/de/services.html and 404s, while "English" points at services.html,
which resolves back to /de/services.html. Cause: build_lang() only inserts a
switcher "if not soup.find(class_='langsel')", and the English source page
already has one, so the localised switcher is copied verbatim instead of being
rebuilt per language. Fix that condition when unfreezing.

